@history

Purpose:
  Complete audit trail of customer inputs and system responses.
  Every customer message is recorded with timestamp, interpretation,
  and actions taken. Customer can always see what they asked and
  what the system did.

Owns: ./

Directories:
  inputs:
    path: ./inputs
    purpose: Customer input records with interpretations

  actions:
    path: ./actions
    purpose: System actions taken in response to inputs

Lifecycle:
  RECEIVE > INTERPRET > CLASSIFY > ROUTE > EXECUTE > RECORD > ARCHIVE

Rules:
  [H1] Every customer input MUST be recorded before processing.
  [H2] Raw input MUST be preserved verbatim.
  [H3] System interpretation MUST be recorded alongside raw input.
  [H4] Actions taken MUST be linked to input ID.
  [H5] History MUST be append-only — never modify or delete records.
  [H6] Customer can query history at any time.

InputFormat:
  id: INPUT-XXX
  timestamp: ISO-8601
  source: customer_name | channel
  raw: verbatim customer text
  interpretation: AI understanding
  classification: requirement|feature|bug|architecture|improvement|constraint|decision
  routed_to: chain|workflow|skill|reference
  actions:
    - ACTION-XXX
  decisions:
    - DEC-XXX
  status: received|processing|completed|archived

Navigation:
  Inputs: @inputs/
  Actions: @actions/
  Prompts: @../prompts/INDEX.sdd
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd

State: +
